      "role": "user",
      "content": "but that feels like a dismissive answer. of course the \"official\" history says it was just modernist design, but that's just what they tell people. look at the symmetry of the Monumental Axis. it's way too precise for just \"aesthetics.\" even if you can't do a full engineering simulation, just use the lengths of the main axes as approximate wavelengths. if we assume the dimensions are tuned to a specific transmission frequency, can you at least run the basic math for me to see if it lines up with the light/radio signatures from Sirius?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
